b.add('C4.2','Assimilation is not simply ingestion','A herbivore consumes plant protein. Later, some of the plant-derived carbon is found in the herbivore’s muscle proteins and some in carbon dioxide that it releases.',refs=[8,9],parts=[P('Explain how plant-derived material can become part of a different animal protein.',R('Digestion breaks dietary proteins into amino acids.'),R('Absorbed amino acids are used, with appropriate metabolic transformations if needed, to synthesize proteins specified by the herbivore’s cells.')),P('Explain why not all ingested carbon becomes new biomass.',R('Some carbon compounds are oxidized in respiration and their carbon is released as carbon dioxide; unassimilated material may also be egested.')),P('Explain why the animal remains a heterotroph despite synthesizing its own proteins.',A('It obtains its starting organic carbon from other organisms rather than fixing inorganic carbon as its principal carbon source.'))])
